  "case_id": "door_front_clearance__schependomlaan",
  "rule": "The area in front of every door must be free of building components.\nSource: rule 'Clearance in Front of Doors' of the EC3-2026 rule catalogue: This rule checks there is enough clearance in front of doors.\nBenchmark convention: the free area is a box directly in front of the door opening, on the side to which the door opens. It is as wide and as high as the door and as deep as the door is wide, shrunk by 50 mm on each side so that components merely touching it do not count. A door fails when any building component other than a space (walls, curtain walls, slabs, floor finishes and other coverings, columns, doors, windows, stairs, railings, furniture, building services or other objects) intersects its free area.\n\nLabel every door.\nReport the GlobalId of every element (modelled as IfcDoor) that does NOT satisfy this requirement.",
